    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40453" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί-παστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sprinkled over</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίπασται τευθίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philox.
					2.16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίπαστον, τό</span>, a kind of <i>cake with comfits</i> (or the
				like ) <i>upon it</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1089
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				130.3
			</span></i>; but (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακον</span>), 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίπασμα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Hum.</u>
				5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				11.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>.</div>
